Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day
first. The fix is queued.

**Update (2026-10-31):** Detailed triage split #4471 into two distinct GitHub issues:
- **Issue #1 (379 reports):** Backend parser month-first assumption across 11 day-first tenants.
- **Issue #2 (33 reports):** Frontend booking-v3 MM/DD/YYYY placeholder hint across 3 day-first tenants.
See full analysis in [4471-split](/kb/incidents/4471-split).

<Callout>
Known. Split into Issue #1 (parser: 379 reports) and Issue #2 (hint: 33 reports).
</Callout>

